I am sitting at my desk again.
I open my laptop.
We have to write the code for the new project.
Jonas comes over to me.
He gets a chair and sits down next to me.
"Did you get the data from Nele?" Jonas asks.
"Yes, I have saved everything," I answer.
I begin with the work and type.
We look at the screen together.
Suddenly the program shows an error.
"A name here is wrong," says Jonas.
We read the code again.
"I programmed the function incorrectly," I say.
I correct the error immediately.
Jonas smiles.
"But errors like that always happen."
I nod in agreement.
"You never stop learning," I answer.
We test the code and now everything works perfectly.
